  "description": "Lets a React, Preact, Solid, Vue, Svelte, Angular or Lit component be an ordinary Rask component in a C# app. Derive a component from ReactComponent, PreactComponent, SolidComponent, VueComponent, SvelteComponent, AngularComponent or LitComponent, drop the front-end file beside it, and its props are declared in C# — the generator emits the TypeScript interface the file imports, so renaming a C# property stops the front end compiling. Callbacks re-enter C#, and the live diff treats the island's subtree as opaque, because those nodes belong to its own renderer.",
